From 3333333333333333333333333333333333333333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Jul 2026 14:30:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] androidmedia: force JNI codec backend (disable NDK AMediaCodec)

THROWAWAY / A-B test. gstamc prefers the NDK AMediaCodec backend when
media/NdkMediaCodec.h is present; on Android <10 file playback this backend
appears not to back-pressure the decoder (hardware decode races to EOS and
the video sink renders ~0 frames), whereas the JNI backend (used by the 1.20
build) paces correctly. Disable the NDK backend at build time so gstamc uses
the JNI backend, to confirm the regression is in the NDK codec path.

The plugin explicitly supports building without NdkMediaCodec.h ("doesn't
affect compatibility with older Android versions"), so this is a supported
JNI-only configuration. Revert by flipping `false and` back off.
---
 subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build | 8 +-
 1 file changed

diff --git a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/androidmedia/meson.build
@@ -83,7 +83,13 @@
 # Build an Ndk support if its headers exists. We don't actually link into it
 # but use only type definations (and then rely on dlopen and dlsym), so this
 # doesn't affect compatibility with older Android versions.
-if cc.check_header('media/NdkMediaCodec.h')
+#
+# THROWAWAY (force JNI codec backend for an A/B test): the leading `false and`
+# disables the NDK AMediaCodec backend so gstamc falls back to the JNI backend
+# (as on pre-NDK Android / the gstreamer 1.20 build). Flip back to just
+# `cc.check_header(...)` to restore NDK. See VIVI investigation into 1.26
+# playContent file-playback racing to EOS.
+if false and cc.check_header('media/NdkMediaCodec.h')
   androidmedia_sources += ndk_sources
   extra_cargs += [ '-DHAVE_NDKMEDIA' ]
   extra_deps += [ cc.find_library('android', required : true) ]
